    {
      "id": "Utb7Q_lhK8_ZhsUNoxzC9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 610.829552650188,
      "y": 1131.3801366959956,
      "width": 1332.379150390625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "QOFfJRTb_umlQjgDTG_xM"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 785637097,
      "version": 1401,
      "versionNonce": 1143431239,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1748271177506,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Explanation: The engine (could be one or more class) will depend on an EntityStore and a SystemsRunner, the EntityStore is responsible\nto store and query all the entities based on a set of components efficiently - these will then be passed to the systems runner to \ndo execute any logic (custom or builtin). The builtin ones will include but are not limited to a RendererSystem, CollisionSystem and \nInputSystem - they are pretty much self explanatory.\n\nThe RendererSystem will depend on the EngineUIRenderer, responsible to use ImGUI to render all the UI related to the engine itself\nand the SceneRenderer will render the actual game scene) - both will have to use the VulkanDriver for utilities methods such as creating\nand updating buffers or anything else related to vulkan. The RendererSystem will also use the VulkanDriver to initalize the drive and \nperform any opertaion on the Vulkan layer that is not specific to either EngineUIRenderer or SceneRenderer.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Explanation: The engine (could be one or more class) will depend on an EntityStore and a SystemsRunner, the EntityStore is responsible\nto store and query all the entities based on a set of components efficiently - these will then be passed to the systems runner to \ndo execute any logic (custom or builtin). The builtin ones will include but are not limited to a RendererSystem, CollisionSystem and \nInputSystem - they are pretty much self explanatory.\n\nThe RendererSystem will depend on the EngineUIRenderer, responsible to use ImGUI to render all the UI related to the engine itself\nand the SceneRenderer will render the actual game scene) - both will have to use the VulkanDriver for utilities methods such as creating\nand updating buffers or anything else related to vulkan. The RendererSystem will also use the VulkanDriver to initalize the drive and \nperform any opertaion on the Vulkan layer that is not specific to either EngineUIRenderer or SceneRenderer.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
